# Force LF line endings on every checkout (all OSes).
#
# Why: the Windows-only shipped html/ rides the cross-OS `webapp-dist`
# actions/cache, whose key is hashFiles() over working-tree bytes
# (src/apps/desktop/**). Without this file, a Windows git with
# core.autocrlf=true (Git for Windows default) checks out CRLF while
# Linux checks out LF -- same commit, different bytes, different key,
# restore ALWAYS misses on Windows, dist/ is absent, build.zig skips
# zig-out/bin/html, and the bundle gate fails. Attributes override any
# runner's core.autocrlf, so all three cells hash identical bytes.
#
# Safe here: the repo is LF-pure (no tracked CRLF) and has no .bat/.cmd
# files (the only common type that requires CRLF). .ps1/.sh/.zig/.vue/.ts
# are all LF-safe -- and .sh REQUIRES LF.
* text=auto eol=lf
